<% desk = @desk; progress = desk.progress; next_day = desk.next_day; next_task = desk.next_task
   this_week = desk.this_week_days; focus_days = desk.focus_days; tasks = desk.focus_tasks
   week_state = desk.week_period(desk.focus_week).state
   menu = []
   if @can_write_finance
     menu << ['Add expense', new_finance_expense_path]
     menu << ['Add vendor payment', new_finance_vendor_payment_path]
   end
   menu << ['Add follow-up', new_reconciliation_follow_up_path] if @can_write_reports %>
<div class="space-y-8 books-desk">
  <%= page_header 'Close & review', subtitle: 'Finish each day, then each week, then lock the period.', menu: menu do %>
    <% if @can_write_finance %><span class="inline-flex" <%= tour_anchor('record') %>><%= link_to 'Import bank statement', bank_statements_path, class: 'btn-ghost' %></span><% end %>
  <% end %>

  <section class="desk-next section-card" aria-labelledby="desk-next-title" <%= tour_anchor('next') %>>
    <div class="desk-next-body">
      <% if next_day %>
        <% stage = next_day.next_stage %>
        <h2 id="desk-next-title" class="section-title"><%= books_desk_stage_action(stage) %></h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm"><strong><%= next_day.day.strftime('%A, %b %-d') %></strong> · <%= stage.label %>: <%= stage.detail %></p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <%= link_to books_desk_stage_action(stage), books_desk_stage_path(next_day.day, stage), class: 'btn-primary' %>
          <%= link_to 'Open the whole day', "#day-#{next_day.day.iso8601}", class: 'btn-ghost' %>
        </div>
      <% elsif next_task %>
        <p class="eyebrow text-olive">Days are done · weekly chore next</p>
        <h2 id="desk-next-title" class="section-title mt-1"><%= next_task.title %></h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm"><%= next_task.detail %></p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><%= link_to books_desk_task_action(next_task), books_desk_task_path(next_task), class: 'btn-primary' %></div>
      <% elsif (period_step = desk.next_period_step) %>
        <% close, task = period_step %>
        <p class="eyebrow text-olive">Days and week are done · <%= close.kind_label.downcase %> end next</p>
        <h2 id="desk-next-title" class="section-title mt-1"><%= close.label %>: <%= task.title.sub(/\A./, &:downcase) %></h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm"><%= task.detail %></p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><%= link_to(task.key == :lock ? "Lock #{close.label}" : books_desk_task_action(task), books_desk_task_path(task), class: 'btn-primary') %></div>
      <% else %>
        <p class="eyebrow text-fern">All caught up</p>
        <h2 id="desk-next-title" class="section-title mt-1">The books are clean</h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm">Days, the selected week’s chores and the latest month, quarter and year are all done. Current-week approvals wait until the week ends.</p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="desk-progress" aria-label="Progress">
      <p class="stat-label">Steps done</p>
      <p class="stat-value-sm mt-1"><%= progress[:steps_done] %> <span class="text-sm text-mocha">of <%= progress[:steps] %></span></p>
      <div class="desk-meter mt-2" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="<%= progress[:steps] %>" aria-valuenow="<%= progress[:steps_done] %>" aria-label="Cleanup steps done">
        <span style="width: <%= progress[:steps].zero? ? 0 : (progress[:steps_done] * 100 / progress[:steps]) %>%"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-mocha"><%= progress[:up_to_date] %> of <%= pluralize(progress[:days], 'day') %> up to date</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <details class="desk-findings card" id="desk-findings" <%= tour_anchor('findings') %>>
    <summary class="desk-findings-summary disclosure-trigger">
      <span class="section-title">What needs reconciliation</span>
      <span class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="<%= @findings.square_missing.count.zero? ? 'pill-fern' : 'pill-rose' %>">Square · <%= @findings.square_missing.count %> without payment</span>
        <span class="<%= @findings.unpaid_invoices.empty? ? 'pill-fern' : 'pill-rose' %>">SwipeSimple · <%= pluralize(@findings.unpaid_invoices.size, 'unpaid invoice') %></span>
      </span>
    </summary>
    <div class="px-5 pb-5"><%= render 'shared/reconciliation_findings', findings: @findings %></div>
  </details>

  <% if this_week.any? %>
    <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="desk-this-week" <%= tour_anchor('this_week') %>>
      <div class="card-head"><div><h2 id="desk-this-week" class="section-title">This week so far</h2><p class="card-hint">Today is still open and appears tomorrow.</p></div></div>
      <div class="space-y-3"><%= render partial: 'books_desks/day', collection: this_week, as: :row %></div>
    </section>
  <% end %>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="desk-focus-week" <%= tour_anchor('week') %>>
    <div class="card-head">
      <div>
        <h2 id="desk-focus-week" class="section-title"><%= desk.focus_week == desk.current_week - 7 ? 'Last week' : 'Earlier week' %> · <%= desk.focus_label %></h2>
        <p class="card-hint">Week approval: <strong><%= { pending: 'not approved yet', changed: 'changed since approval', approved: 'approved', approved_with_exceptions: 'approved with exceptions', needs_attention: 'needs attention' }.fetch(week_state, week_state.to_s.humanize) %></strong></p>
      </div>
      <nav class="card-head-actions date-stepper" aria-label="Choose a week">
        <%= link_to '‹', books_desk_path(week: desk.previous_week.iso8601, anchor: 'desk-focus-week'), class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm', rel: 'prev', aria: { label: 'Earlier week' }, title: 'Earlier week' %>
        <% if desk.next_week %><%= link_to 'Last week', books_desk_path, class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm' %><%= link_to '›', books_desk_path(week: desk.next_week.iso8601, anchor: 'desk-focus-week'), class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm', rel: 'next', aria: { label: 'Later week' }, title: 'Later week' %><% end %>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <div class="desk-week-grid">
      <section class="section-card desk-chores" aria-labelledby="desk-chores-title">
        <%= section_heading 'Weekly chores', hint: "#{tasks.count { |t| t.done? && !t.optional }} of #{tasks.count { |t| !t.optional }} done", level: :h3 %>
        <ol class="space-y-2">
          <% tasks.each do |task| %>
            <li class="desk-task" data-state="<%= task.state %>">
              <span class="desk-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><%= books_desk_glyph(task.state) %></span>
              <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="font-semibold"><%= task.title %><span class="sr-only"> · <%= books_desk_state_label(task.state) %></span><% if task.optional %> <span class="pill-taupe">Optional</span><% end %></p>
                <p class="text-xs text-mocha"><%= task.detail %></p>
                <% unless task.done? %><%= link_to books_desk_task_action(task), books_desk_task_path(task), class: 'mt-1 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-olive-deep hover:underline' %><% end %>
              </div>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ol>
      </section>
      <div class="space-y-3 min-w-0"><%= render partial: 'books_desks/day', collection: focus_days, as: :row %></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="desk-period-end" <%= tour_anchor('periods') %>>
    <%= section_heading 'Month, quarter and year end', hint: 'Finish each period, then lock it so history cannot be edited by accident.' %>
    <div class="card row-list">
      <% desk.period_closes.each do |close| %>
        <% close_task = close.tasks.find { |t| !t.done? && !t.optional } %>
        <article class="row-item" aria-labelledby="close-<%= close.kind %>">
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <h3 id="close-<%= close.kind %>" class="font-semibold text-ink"><%= close.label %></h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-taupe"><%= close.kind_label %> end<% if close_task %> · <%= close_task.detail %><% end %></p>
            <details class="explainer mt-1">
              <summary class="explainer-summary">Steps</summary>
              <ol class="mt-2 space-y-1.5">
                <% close.tasks.each do |task| %>
                  <li class="desk-task text-sm" data-state="<%= task.state %>"><span class="desk-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><%= books_desk_glyph(task.state) %></span><span class="min-w-0"><%= task.title %><span class="sr-only"> · <%= books_desk_state_label(task.state) %></span><% if task.optional %> <span class="text-xs text-mocha">(optional)</span><% end %></span></li>
                <% end %>
              </ol>
            </details>
          </div>
          <div class="row-item-end">
            <% if close.locked? && close.lock_current? %><span class="pill-fern">Locked</span>
            <% elsif close.locked? %><span class="pill-rose">Changed after lock</span>
            <% else %><span class="pill-taupe"><%= close.done_count %> of <%= close.total_count %> done</span><% end %>
            <% if close_task %><%= link_to(close_task.key == :lock ? "Lock #{close.label}" : books_desk_task_action(close_task), books_desk_task_path(close_task), class: 'btn-ghost btn-sm') %><% end %>
          </div>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3" aria-labelledby="desk-housekeeping">
    <div class="card-head">
      <div><h2 id="desk-housekeeping" class="section-title">Housekeeping</h2><p class="card-hint">Imports, payments, originals and backups for the last 30 days.</p></div>
    </div>
    <%= turbo_frame_tag 'books-desk-checks', src: checks_books_desk_path, loading: :lazy do %>
      <p class="card card-pad text-sm text-mocha" role="status">Loading…</p>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <details class="explainer card card-pad">
    <summary class="explainer-summary font-semibold">How the routine works</summary>
    <div class="mt-3 grid gap-6 text-sm md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Every day (about 5 minutes)</h3>
        <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5">
          <% BooksDesk::STAGES.each do |_key, (label, hint)| %><li><strong><%= label %>.</strong> <%= hint %></li><% end %>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-mocha">The oldest unfinished day comes first, so a backlog is worked in order. Rupert shows what is done and opens the right page for whatever is next; nothing here changes a record by itself. A day can be approved on its own or as part of its week. Closing or approving “with exceptions” counts as done, with your note on record.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="card-title">Once a week (Monday works well)</h3>
        <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li>Download the bank statement CSV and upload it.</li>
          <li>Say what each withdrawal was: an expense, a vendor payment or nothing to record.</li>
          <li>Add any money out the bank did not show.</li>
          <li>Clear overdue follow-ups.</li>
          <li>Approve the week.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-mocha">Sources, currencies and locations are never added together. Unavailable amounts are not zero.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <h3 class="card-title">Month, quarter and year end</h3>
        <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5">
          <li><strong>Month:</strong> every day approved, statements reach month end, bank lines decided, follow-ups closed, monthly money report saved, then lock the month.</li>
          <li><strong>Quarter:</strong> all three months locked and the quarterly report saved, then lock the quarter.</li>
          <li><strong>Year:</strong> all four quarters locked, the yearly report saved and an off-host backup current, then lock the year.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-mocha">Locks keep a dated archive of the period’s totals (<%= link_to 'period locks', period_locks_path, class: 'font-semibold text-olive-deep hover:underline' %>). A lock makes expenses, vendor payments, bank-line decisions, reviews, closes and approvals inside the period read-only. Reopening needs a store administrator and a written reason; both are kept in a tamper-evident ledger. Originals, archives and saved reports are never deleted automatically.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
</div>
